msgid "Full changelog"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is the end of the year (again) and here comes our last release of the "
"year, 2.15.1.Final.\n"
"We had 9 minor releases this year (starting with 2.7 in February) and so "
"many micros.\n"
"We made tremendous progress on Quarkus itself and the activity in the "
"ecosystem of extensions has been extremely prolific."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This version contains bugfixes and documentation improvements on top of our "
"2.15.0.Final release.\n"
"It is a recommended upgrade for anyone already using 2.15."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are not already using 2.15, please refer to https://github.com/"
"quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-2.15[our migration guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Happy holidays and see you next year for more Quarkus goodness!"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can get https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/releases/tag/2.15.1."
"Final[the full changelog of 2.15.1.Final on GitHub]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Come Join Us"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We value your feedback a lot so please report bugs, ask for improvements... "
"Let's build something great together!"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are a Quarkus user or just curious, don't be shy and join our "
"welcoming community:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"provide feedback on https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues[GitHub];"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"craft some code and https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pulls[push a PR];"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"discuss with us on https://quarkusio.zulipchat.com/[Zulip] and on the https:/"
"/groups.google.com/d/forum/quarkus-dev[mailing list];"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"ask your questions on https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/"
"quarkus[Stack Overflow]."
msgstr ""
